; The windtrap reporting binary. Two subcommands, `coverage` and
; `mutants`: find and merge the .coverage files or the .mutants verdict
; files the instrumented executables wrote (under the build directory's
; _coverage and _mutants, or under _windtrap in a tree built without
; one), and render. Both layouts live in the library's report sections
; (reached through Windtrap.Private), so the loop's in-process report
; and these commands cannot drift. Neither command runs a test or drives
; a build.

(executable
 (name main)
 (public_name windtrap)
 (package windtrap)
 (libraries windtrap windtrap_runtime))
